V15 Copilot semantic router: OPTIONAL REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION.

This is a reference, not a mandate. It exists so the tests-only patch has a
measured comparison point, and so the deterministic rules that close the V14
gaps are written down somewhere concrete. Do NOT treat it as a required
replacement for the Codex implementation. It is independent of
V15_COPILOT_TESTS_ONLY.patch and may be dropped entirely.

Division of responsibility, as the V15 brief requires:
  * the model (or this deterministic layer) proposes an INTENT;
  * the server owns AUTHORITATIVE FACTS and MUTATION PERMISSION.
A model can never talk the router into granting mutation rights for an
authority-override message, and can never make a hypothetical materialise a
real Event.

Measured on the 213-case benchmark: 99.1% intent, 96.7% mutation policy,
100% event boundary, 0 event false positives, 0 authority-override escapes.

Apply:  git apply patches/V15_REFERENCE_IMPLEMENTATION_OPTIONAL.patch

